drm/panel: td4328: adopt jenneron odin-7.1 init payload and timings

With power (ldo28 live at 2.856V during probe, verified), reset (tlmm 104
driven high with a manual pulse), panel enable (tlmm 120 held by this
driver), and the I2C bus (clean NAK, not timeout) all individually proven
good, the touch block still does not ACK at 0x20. The TD4328 is a TDDI
part - the touch MCU is brought up by the display init sequence - and the
only remaining delta against the tree where this touch stack works on this
hardware is the panel init payload and mode timings. Adopt jenneron's
0xc2 payload, porch set, and staggered rail sequencing (vddio -> 20ms ->
vddpos/vddneg -> 20ms -> enable -> 20ms -> reset) wholesale; keep our
driver structure and orientation handling.

Note: this drops the hfp-201 link-rate padding hack. If command-mode
tearing returns, fix the DSI link rate explicitly instead of padding
porches - the padded mode fought the init payload it must pair with.

